# The declaration line of an own place runs at every reach (the author 2026-11-11, R12; plan M11 5a, B5, B10): it writes
# what stands in its slot -- the place's own cell, the literal 5 -- so each launch of Self ends with x = 5, although
# the line above it added 1.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# Self is launched over itself in the code of main, which reads first and second after each launch; self_x is the x of
# Self at the end.
sub: main () (
    Self:
        x := x + 1
        int: x 5
    int: first 0
    int: second 0
)
    call: Self
    first := Self\x
    call: Self
    second := Self\x
main()
int: first main\data\first
int: second main\data\second
int: self_x main\data\Self\x
